      "description": {
        "fun": "A tantrum-prone baby that drinks dirty water, filters it into poison, then changes the poison's chemistry to make a weak electric charge. You might want to cuddle it, but its skin leaks poison and leaves huggers tingling, so it's best admired from a distance. It was the first new baby Pokémon since Generation 4.",
        "guide": "A baby Electric and Poison-type lizard Pokémon that filters dirty water into poison and turns it into weak electricity. Toxel is selfish and attention-seeking. It evolves into Toxtricity, in Amped or Low Key Form depending on its nature.",
        "tagline": "A tingly, tantrum-throwing baby you shouldn't hug",
        "sources": [
          {
            "title": "Bulbapedia: Toxel (Pokémon)",
            "url": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Toxel_(Pok%C3%A9mon)"
          }
        ]
      },
      "branches": {
        "text": "Toxel's nature decides, and a Mint can't change it. Natures such as Hardy, Adamant, Jolly and Naive give the guitar-playing Amped Form; natures such as Bold, Timid, Modest and Calm give the bass-playing Low Key Form.",
        "sources": [
          {
